  "definition": "Lithium, here referring to lithium carbonate, is a pharmacologic substance with mood-stabilizing and antimanic effects. It acts on nerve-cell signaling and neurotransmitter-related processes, although the exact way it produces its mood-stabilizing effect is not fully established.",
